// XFAIL: RT-42b: `m[0] = 0xFF` through a `&mut str` builds and writes a byte: an invalid String in safe code (open)
// A str is not indexed by an integer (rustc: error[E0277]: the type
// `str` cannot be indexed by `{integer}`), and its bytes are not
// written from safe code. vole takes `m[0]` of a `&mut str` as a byte
// and writes 0xFF over the first byte of "éa": the String's bytes are
// [255, 169, 97], and from_utf8 refuses them (vole prints `[255, 169,
// 97] false` and exits 0). (vole also reads `s[0]` of a `&str` as its
// first byte, which breaks no str; the write does.) Found with RT-42:
// the checker's str rules match only `str_type`.
// ERROR: error[
// ERROR: line 14,
fn main(gpa: Gpa) {
    let mut x = String::from_in("éa", gpa);
    let mut m: &mut str = x.as_mut_str();
    m[0] = 0xFF;
    println("{:?} {}", x.as_bytes(), std::str::from_utf8(x.as_bytes()).is_ok());
}
